    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d90">

                <pb facs="0155" n="63" sameAs="frus:frus1943CairoTehran/pg63"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt
                    Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Winant</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the President</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d90-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-11-02">2 November 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Personal and secret to the President from Winant.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <p>1. If you travel I would like to meet with you. There would be no objection here
                    and my transportation could be easily arranged. Never <pb facs="0156" n="64"
                        xml:id="pg64"/> attending conferences has put me outside the lines of
                    communications and has cut down my usefulness to you.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d90-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d90-f1-content">
                <p>Sent to Washington by the United States Military Attaché, London, and forwarded
                    by the White House Map Room to Roosevelt
                    at Hyde Park.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
